--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What we build ON, and do not redistribute
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`Dockerfile` starts `FROM public.ecr.aws/e1h7x4a2/plow-cloud-agents:base-...`,
the Plow base image built by https://github.com/plow-pbc/plow-openclaw-agent. We
did not copy its code and we do not ship it. It is a build input, like a
compiler.

  **The base image carries no declared licence.** The GitHub API reports
  `license: None` for plow-pbc/plow-openclaw-agent, and its `owners-mac` and
  `google-workspace` skills carry no licence header either. We build on it and
  ship none of it. We also copy none of it: our `COPY skills/ /opt/plow/skills/`
  merges our three skills in beside the base's and leaves the base's where the
  base put them. If you need those two skills under a licence, ask Plow.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What we read at runtime, and do not redistribute
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `plow-wiki` skill, from https://github.com/plow-pbc/plow-wiki (Apache-2.0).
We do not vendor it. The owner installs the `wiki` Latch plugin on their Mac, the
plugin publishes its own `skill.md` there, and the agent reads it at runtime with
`plow_list_skills` / `plow_read_skill` — the same path the base's `owners-mac`
skill uses for anything the Mac publishes. If the plugin is not installed, this
agent has no long-term memory and says so; it does not fall back to a copy of
the skill baked into this image.

